sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Gateway as Gateway API (Envoy)<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.3
    participant KRBAC as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant VLLM as vllm-gaudi Container<br/>8000/TCP HTTP
    participant HPU as Intel Gaudi HPU<br/>PCIe/HCCL
    participant PeerHPU as Peer HPU Workers<br/>HCCL/RDMA
    participant S3 as Model Storage<br/>(S3/PVC/HF Hub)<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over Client,S3: Flow 1: Model Loading at Startup

    VLLM->>S3: GET model weights<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS 1.2+<br/>Auth: AWS IAM / HF Token / SA
    S3-->>VLLM: Model artifacts (weights, tokenizer)
    VLLM->>HPU: Load model to HPU device memory<br/>PCIe / HCCL
    Note over VLLM,HPU: HPU Graph compilation<br/>per unique tensor shape<br/>(bucketing reduces recompilation)

    Note over Client,S3: Flow 2: Model Inference Request

    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS 1.3<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    Gateway->>KRBAC: Forward request<br/>HTTPS/8443 TLS<br/>SubjectAccessReview
    Note over KRBAC: Validates token via<br/>Kubernetes RBAC
    KRBAC->>VLLM: Forward request<br/>HTTP/8000 (localhost)<br/>No auth (trusted sidecar)

    Note over VLLM: vLLM OpenAI API Server<br/>processes request through<br/>vllm_gaudi plugin pipeline

    VLLM->>HPU: Execute inference<br/>Attention (FusedSDPA)<br/>Model forward pass

    alt Multi-Card Inference (Tensor/Pipeline Parallelism)
        VLLM->>PeerHPU: Distribute computation<br/>HCCL/RDMA (dynamic ports)<br/>No encryption
        PeerHPU->>HPU: All-reduce / All-gather<br/>HCCL collective ops
    end

    HPU-->>VLLM: Inference result (logits/tokens)

    Note over VLLM: Token sampling<br/>(with optional speculative decode)

    VLLM-->>KRBAC: JSON response
    KRBAC-->>Gateway: Forward response
    Gateway-->>Client: JSON response<br/>(OpenAI-compatible format)

    Note over Client,S3: Flow 3: Health Check

    Client->>Gateway: GET /health<br/>HTTPS/443
    Gateway->>VLLM: GET /health<br/>HTTP/8000
    VLLM-->>Gateway: 200 OK
    Gateway-->>Client: 200 OK
